WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
- We are headed to go meet up with my dad

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.563
who I haven't seen in about eight years.

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:10.210
(piano music)

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.820
I wish I had a very clear sign

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.853
of why we didn't talk, or what happened,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.800
there was never a big blow up.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.243
We just stopped talking.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.570
That's probably the
most painful part of it.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.623
Apparently I wasn't enough
for my dad to stay around.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.560
I remember being so nervous yesterday

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.260
that he wasn't gonna show up.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.913
I mean I bought a plane ticket,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.160
arranged all this, and I
still was sitting there

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.180
yesterday like he's not gonna come.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.955
It's just weird to have a person

00:00:39.955 --> 00:00:42.823
who is so deeply connected to me,

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.050
feel so distant at the same time.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.400
He would promise to show up,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.860
and he would say he would do things,

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.710
and then wouldn't come, or just like,

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.872
wouldn't call me back,
or just would disappear,

00:00:51.872 --> 00:00:54.774
like I feel like I should know this man.

00:00:54.774 --> 00:00:58.290
And to be honest, he truly is a stranger.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.050
I don't know that we will
leave this conversation

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.273
being this happy father and son.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.890
I don't know that we will
ever have a real relationship,

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.853
but, the worse case scenario
is more of the same.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.633
It just feels, it feels more real.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.300
More real than I thought
it was gonna feel.

00:01:19.507 --> 00:01:22.693
I just, am nervous.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.550
I don't, I don't know
why, I don't feel like

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.723
I have a reason to be nervous, but,

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.943
it's just, feels very nerve-wracking.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.720
My dad has been in and out of my life.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.003
Mostly out.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.963
He's not a bad person, he
just wasn't the best dad.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.350
I've moved on, like,

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.500
I don't hold a lot of anger

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.720
or resentment towards him about it.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.850
It's a conversation I wanna have

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.700
and just kind of get to know him

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.230
because I feel like I missed
out on getting to know him.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.140
One specific memory I have that was

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.680
just us building like, a fort of leaves.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.410
We were at my grandmother's house.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.420
We hung out all day,
like so long that we got

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.370
locked out of my grandmother's
house 'cause like,

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.820
my grandmother left, and we
were just like, hanging out.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.120
And that's most of my
memories with my dad.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.733
I feel like the older I got,
the less time I spent with him.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.780
The goal of today, for me, is
to find some level of closure

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.490
and kind of get to know myself better

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.210
by getting to know my dad

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.810
and getting to know some
of the pain I went through.

00:02:25.505 --> 00:02:26.422
- Hey, Dad.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.777
- How are you doing?

00:02:28.921 --> 00:02:31.171
I missed you, I missed you.

00:02:31.977 --> 00:02:32.923
You okay?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.000
- Yeah, I'm fine.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.280
Um, it just, it's been, I dunno.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.073
It just, I just, nerve -- I don't know.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:41.433
- You're nervous.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:42.580
- Yeah.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.910
I am happy to see you.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:44.743
You look good.

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:45.800
- You do, too.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.800
- I wish, I dunno, I put on some weight.

00:02:47.813 --> 00:02:49.350
- You look good, though.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.350
You carry it well.

00:02:50.684 --> 00:02:51.684
- Thank you.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.080
The older I get, I think,
'cause I know I went through

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.540
a period where I was
like, very angry with you.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.490
- Mm-hmm, I'm sure.

00:02:58.668 --> 00:02:59.830
And you have every right to be.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.180
You have every right to be.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.903
That's why, when you
called, I cried, Ryann.

00:03:04.626 --> 00:03:06.410
I cried for a minute, 'cause it was like,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.110
I've been praying to God about it,

00:03:08.157 --> 00:03:10.343
and I got it, family has to come first.

00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:12.890
And it took me awhile to get that.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.253
54 years to get that.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.313
But I got it.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.680
- For me, I feel like
there's just a lot --

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.513
- It is a lot.

00:03:18.513 --> 00:03:20.420
- ... to unpack.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.500
I feel like in order for me
to like, grow as a person,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.690
and like, be a better person,

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.670
I have to just talk to
you about just, stuff.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.073
Just, starting like,
what, what do you think,

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.643
like, I guess, a good dad is?

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.930
- I think a guy, a good dad

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.140
is someone that you can count on.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.190
Someone that's there.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.170
You have to be there.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:38.790
And it's funny when you
say that, because you know,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.620
as a kid growing up, you know Grandpa,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.460
you know I ain't see, growing up with him,

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.440
being the way he was.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.540
I always said I was gonna be a better dad.

00:03:46.008 --> 00:03:49.673
Turned out, getting caught up
in the other things, Ryann.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.400
- I think that like,
pain becomes more real

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.403
the older you get.

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:54.427
- Yes, it does.

00:03:54.427 --> 00:03:56.900
- And it's, it would've been nice to have

00:03:58.296 --> 00:04:00.023
you there, I mean like.

00:04:00.348 --> 00:04:01.900
I'm not mad,
- you're right.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.733
- It's just like, real.

00:04:02.733 --> 00:04:04.220
It would've been nice to have --

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.900
- You want an answer for that, right?

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.580
- Not necessarily an answer, I just want,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.773
like, and I'm ready for
you not to have like,

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:11.970
a direct answer.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.200
Like, 'cause if it's "I
don't know," I get it.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.080
- No, it's not gonna, I'm
gonna say I don't know,

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.320
but all I can tell you,
they're gonna be pieces, Ryann.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.320
That's all they are.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:19.343
I messed up.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.593
I wasn't a good father to you guys.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:22.703
I wasn't.

00:04:22.703 --> 00:04:23.850
I should've been there.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.260
I missed a lot and I can't get that back.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.700
And that's something I have to live with

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.900
for the rest of my life.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.090
I was smoking, on drugs, I
was doing all kinds of things

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.967
when you -- I wasn't in the
right place for you guys.

00:04:33.967 --> 00:04:36.223
I didn't see you graduate.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.313
College, either.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.370
I can't get that back, Ryann.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.313
That hurts.

00:04:41.904 --> 00:04:42.737
It hurts a lot.

00:04:42.737 --> 00:04:43.570
But it's my fault.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.023
I'm not trying to make
excuses for anything.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:48.393
- Like, growing up, I felt like,

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:53.503
because Cameron is a
little, he's a little more,

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.290
like sensitive to your relationship,

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.240
and I think he shows his emotions more.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.903
And then, Mom was always working.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:05.260
And like, a lot of times I felt like

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.720
I had to be the happy one.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.887
- Oh no, don't cry.
- No it's not --

00:05:07.887 --> 00:05:09.061
- Don't do that.

00:05:09.061 --> 00:05:10.115
Don't do that, don't do that.

00:05:10.115 --> 00:05:11.784
Don't don't don't don't.

00:05:11.784 --> 00:05:13.468
Don't do that, don't do that.

00:05:13.468 --> 00:05:15.219
Don't do that, don't do that.

00:05:15.219 --> 00:05:16.438
(crying)

00:05:16.438 --> 00:05:17.271
Don't do that.

00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:18.104
Don't do that.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.107
- It just, sometimes, 'cause
I felt like (sniffling) --

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.610
- It wasn't you.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.297
It had nothing to do with you.
- I know.

00:05:25.297 --> 00:05:26.130
That's not what I'm saying.

00:05:26.648 --> 00:05:29.620
It's just that, it just hurt

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:33.883
because I had to be strong
and happy for everybody.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.823
Because Cameron didn't believe in you,

00:05:37.519 --> 00:05:38.967
and so I had to be like,

00:05:38.967 --> 00:05:41.307
"No, Dad's gonna come through this time."

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.760
and then, Mom didn't believe in you,

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.877
and I had to make sure she was happy.

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:50.530
And it just, it felt like,
and even to this day,

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:54.050
it's hard for me to be
vulnerable with people.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.855
- I'm sorry.
- And not put on a happy face

00:05:55.855 --> 00:06:00.673
all the time because I
feel like I've never had --

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.840
- I'm sorry.
- I feel like I've never

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.023
had someone to be there.

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:10.740
And it would've been nice to have a dad

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:14.263
to just like, allow me to be sad.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.293
- You're right.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:16.850
I wish I could change that, I really,

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.219
if I could do anything to
change it right now, I would.

00:06:19.219 --> 00:06:20.403
- And I --
- But I can't.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.243
- And I get that.

00:06:21.243 --> 00:06:24.620
I'm not, this isn't me
like, attacking, or like -

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.329
I just want you to, and I --

00:06:26.329 --> 00:06:28.810
- Even if you did, I deserve that.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.813
If you did, I deserve that.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.940
There's a lot of times
I wanted to just get up,

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:36.973
just pop up and find you.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.210
Find out where you were.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.410
But I just didn't wanna,

00:06:41.857 --> 00:06:43.560
I just didn't wanna
mess up your life, man.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:44.410
That's the truth.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.953
I can't make you happy, or come
talk to you about something,

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.713
if I don't have me right.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.963
I had to get me right
before I could do anything.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.363
And I did that.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:01.220
Therapy, AA, drugs anon,
I've been through it all.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:04.643
Now I'm here.

00:07:06.114 --> 00:07:07.900
(soda can popping open)

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.660
- We started talking about it earlier,

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.570
I know, 'cause I never, I haven't like,

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.320
told you, I guess in person before.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.070
I assumed you knew, but like,

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.664
I have not come out to you, I guess --

00:07:17.664 --> 00:07:18.730
- No. You haven't.
- ... yet.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.783
Uh, so yeah, like I am
gay, and I didn't like,

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.510
I assumed you knew 'cause
I knew you followed me

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.780
on like, social media.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:27.940
Does that bother you?

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.723
- No, does it not bother me at all.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.080
I feel, I don't feel upset about it.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.010
I feel, as long as he's happy
and he's living the life

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:40.573
the way he wants to live, I love him.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.800
He's my son.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.050
- I know specifically
in the black community,

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.370
and like I remember one of the
things that happened with Mom

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.973
when I told her, she was
just like, scared for me.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.390
And I didn't know if that was ever like --

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.390
- Yes, that's probably one of the reasons

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.990
why I worried about you
down here in LA by yourself.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.029
- I thought here would be
the place to be gay, though.

00:07:59.029 --> 00:07:59.862
I felt like --

00:07:59.862 --> 00:08:00.695
- But I don't look at it like that.

00:08:00.695 --> 00:08:02.270
I look at my son's down
here in a new place,

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.458
and I know you got a few
family people down here,

00:08:04.458 --> 00:08:06.610
but he's in a new place,
and it's just a crazy world

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.600
we live in, Ryann.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.250
This world we live in
today is not the same.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.560
Things are, things are different.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.220
And people try to hurt people

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.447
just because of who they
are and the way they are.

00:08:13.447 --> 00:08:17.710
- You remember, right?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.543
- Mm-hmm.

00:08:18.543 --> 00:08:20.903
- So, okay.

00:08:21.235 --> 00:08:24.740
Her son, I did not realize
this when I was younger,

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:27.720
but the older I got, I realized

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.963
that he molested me as a kid.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.563
And I --

00:08:32.835 --> 00:08:33.668
- What?

00:08:33.668 --> 00:08:35.263
- Okay, I know that it's like, but like,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.250
that's like, I don't know
how to bring this up,

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.150
but I feel like it's something
I feel like you should know.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:45.330
I don't think that, one,
know that I do not blame you

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.220
in any way shape or form,
because you didn't know.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.720
You would've had no way to
know, 'cause I didn't even know.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.943
Now, as an adult looking back,

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.723
I understand that it was
him being inappropriate.

00:08:56.251 --> 00:08:58.863
I don't think I knew what it was as a kid.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.590
- If you didn't know what it was as a kid,

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:01.810
you still supposed to say, "Well Dad" --

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.500
- I didn't, but it didn't,
I didn't know it was wrong.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.020
How I didn't, he would just
kind of like, make me touch him,

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.133
and I didn't, I didn't know.

00:09:11.347 --> 00:09:13.597
And I don't know how I
feel about it, really.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.901
But I just felt like it was something

00:09:15.901 --> 00:09:17.570
that I should just like, let you know.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.840
- Yeah, it is.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:19.673
I'm glad you did.

00:09:19.673 --> 00:09:21.380
That's another example of what I'm saying

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:22.693
about me and my life.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:23.922
Now I'm feeling bad, like
I put you in a position

00:09:23.922 --> 00:09:26.883
and in a situation that
you shouldn't have been in.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.215
Those are things that, you know,

00:09:29.215 --> 00:09:31.100
I learned and I think about it.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.713
I put myself in certain situations

00:09:32.713 --> 00:09:36.660
and I feel like some of the
situations I put myself in

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.945
and some of the things I did,

00:09:37.945 --> 00:09:39.379
'cause it affected my entire life.

00:09:39.379 --> 00:09:40.369
It affected my family, it's affected you,

00:09:40.369 --> 00:09:41.713
it's affected Cameron.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.360
I haven't felt like I
needed a shot of anything --

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.610
- I'm so sorry.
- ... in over, five years,

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:50.993
but that was something.

00:09:52.179 --> 00:09:53.012
- I'm sorry, Dad.
- I'm sorry, Ryann.

00:09:53.012 --> 00:09:53.845
I'm sorry.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:54.863
I'm sorry.

00:09:54.863 --> 00:09:55.696
For that, too.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.581
'Cause that shouldn't have happened.

00:09:58.581 --> 00:10:00.260
Well I'm glad that you could come out,

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.710
you could tell me things now.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.315
I'm hoping this is the start.

00:10:03.315 --> 00:10:04.148
- Yeah.

00:10:04.764 --> 00:10:07.514
(peaceful music)

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:12.663
Today went a lot better
than I thought it would.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.617
- How did you expect it to?

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:17.290
- Well, one, I didn't know
you were gonna show up.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.313
- Well yeah, okay.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:21.033
- I don't know, I didn't know
what to expect, but like,

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.090
I think unfortunately I
had just gotten so used

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:26.410
to expecting the worse,
and I actually just feel

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:28.420
like it went way better.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.680
And I don't know, I'm just,
I'm glad we got to talk.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:31.830
- I'm glad we did, too.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:35.557
I'm hoping this is the beginning
of something totally new.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.323
I'm glad that you don't hate me.

00:10:37.323 --> 00:10:38.156
- No.

00:10:38.156 --> 00:10:39.400
Life is too short to hate.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.230
Regardless of what we went through

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.023
or what our relationship was/is,

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:46.040
I wouldn't exist without you,

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.650
and I find it very hard
to hate someone who,

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.933
for better or worse, made me who I am.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.860
So one of the reasons I wanted to like,

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.660
finish out in nature, was just like,

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:58.490
because one of my fondest memories.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.970
- Memories, mm-hmm.
- Yeah, is with you.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.750
Is like, when we were
playing in the leaves,

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.113
and then we got locked out.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.460
So it was just cool to kinda like,

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.600
I don't know, full circle,
come back to like --

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.433
- Nature.

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:08.266
- Yeah.

00:11:09.165 --> 00:11:11.915
(peaceful music)

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:16.250
I like, I hated the fact that

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:19.293
I really didn't have a
picture of us together.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.313
Like, it would be cool to
like, kind of take a picture.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.640
I just know it sounds cheesy.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:24.473
- No, it's not cheesy.

00:11:24.473 --> 00:11:25.484
No, it's not.

00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:26.317
I wanna take a picture.
- You wanna take a picture.

00:11:26.317 --> 00:11:27.150
A decent picture --
- Okay.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:27.983
- ... with my dad.

00:11:28.549 --> 00:11:29.382
- Get a decent picture.

00:11:29.382 --> 00:11:30.215
- This will be good.

00:11:30.215 --> 00:11:31.060
I'm balding, too, so thanks for that.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:31.940
- Well that's gonna happen.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:32.793
- Ready?
- Yep.

00:11:33.405 --> 00:11:35.490
(picture snaps)

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.713
Good, see?

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.505
I don't know.
- Send that to me.

00:11:38.505 --> 00:11:39.670
- I will.

00:11:39.741 --> 00:11:41.356
I don't know if your phone
will be able to like --

00:11:41.356 --> 00:11:42.972
- No, send it to my email.

00:11:42.972 --> 00:11:44.181
- Okay.
- and I'll get it.

00:11:44.181 --> 00:11:45.249
- 'cause your phone won't
be able to download.

00:11:45.249 --> 00:11:46.913
- No, my phone won't
be able to (laughing).

00:11:47.133 --> 00:11:49.883
(peaceful music)

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.310
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new channel.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.143
- [Offscreen] And now your part.

00:12:12.143 --> 00:12:12.976
- [Both] Subscribe here.

00:12:12.976 --> 00:12:13.973
